WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:11.280
In fact, I've always said that
I don't need to go anywhere,

2
00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:13.520
I don't want to leave Estonia.

3
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.160
Why should I leave,
I have everything in Estonia.

4
00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.160
I have a job, I have friends, a family,
everything is in Estonia.

5
00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:25.600
But then it happened that
at the beginning of 2015,

6
00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:29.960
my employment contract was terminated.

7
00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:34.080
When I started looking
for a new job in Estonia,

8
00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:37.920
I couldn't find anything that I wanted.

9
00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:51.520
GENERATION BEYOND BORDERS

10
00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:56.800
NEW COUNTRY,
NEW OPPORTUNITIES

11
00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:01.320
So we had to decide whether we
should change professions

12
00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:05.080
or start looking abroad,
or what we should do.

13
00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:10.720
But then, at a friend's birthday party,
drunk, I decided,

14
00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:14.440
okay, let's go and see what happens.

15
00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:18.760
At that time, the situation was
favourable, because Kaiti was...

16
00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:20.200
You decided?

17
00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:23.320
Well, I decided,
but you came along with it.

18
00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.360
I wouldn't have left Estonia alone.

19
00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:29.080
Well, since I was at home with Matilda,

20
00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:33.080
it didn't matter to me
where I was at home with the child.

21
00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:37.080
Then we thought, why not?

22
00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:41.240
Yes. So we decided

23
00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:44.720
to go and see,
to try what it was like.

24
00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:47.560
To go on an adventure.
- An adventure, yes.

25
00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.400
I remember leaving Estonia

26
00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:07.120
on August 20, 2010,
the Restoration of Independence Day,

27
00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.720
flags were flying
and I was on my way to the airport,

28
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.520
probably thinking I'd never come back.

29
00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.240
I left with a huge sense of liberation.

30
00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:24.720
Finally I can see the world,

31
00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:28.400
leave this Õismäe and the centre
of Tallinn somehow behind

32
00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:31.680
and I was only happy.

33
00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:35.400
I was anxious mainly for
financial reasons, but when you're 21,

34
00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:38.200
you don't think much
about money or the future.

35
00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:40.400
It's a great feeling of freedom

36
00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:43.720
that you can never go back to
later in life.

37
00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.680
Then real life kicks in.

38
00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:52.480
But when you're in your early 20s,
anything seems possible at that moment.

39
00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:05.360
I was disappointed
with my job in Estonia.

40
00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:13.160
Some personal relationships
had also ended unhappily.

41
00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:19.080
I really wanted a change of scenery.

42
00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:26.360
I like to start from a blank page
and finish some chapters.

43
00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:31.960
It was such an all-encompassing desire.

44
00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:40.400
To live in a somewhat
uncomfortable environment.

45
00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:44.800
Because sharing a small apartment
with several strangers

46
00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:49.280
was not a prospect.

47
00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:51.880
In Estonia, it seems to me that...

48
00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:57.360
Well, I was 26 when I moved to Vienna.

49
00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:01.880
Many of my schoolmates
had already started families.

50
00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:13.560
I think that in Berlin,
like in any big city,

51
00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:17.720
finding a place to live
is very difficult.

52
00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:24.440
Finding something affordable,
or finding anything at all,

53
00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:26.600
is really difficult.

54
00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:32.800
Berlin is a very popular place
for people to go to right now.

55
00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:36.080
I was an au pair for half a year

56
00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:43.080
and since I decided to stay there,
I started looking for a place to live.

57
00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.880
I basically couldn't find one.

58
00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:51.600
I worked as a cleaner for a few months

59
00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:54.760
because I needed to get
some money at some point.

60
00:04:55.080 --> 00:05:00.040
I also started to feel like
I should move back to Estonia.

61
00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:02.160
What am I doing here?

62
00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:08.120
All these self-pitying thoughts
came to mind.

63
00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:26.400
Being away from Estonia for ten years
has been tough in a sense.

64
00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:29.840
In English, there's a saying
'the honeymoon phase',

65
00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:33.800
so the honeymoon phase
definitely passed at some point.

66
00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:38.760
When you've been in the US
for two-three-four-five years,

67
00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:43.320
the novelty slowly wears off
and you're stuck there.

68
00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:46.160
You understand how
this country really works,

69
00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:49.440
or in the case of the US,
you could say it doesn't work.

70
00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:52.400
You compare a lot at every turn.

71
00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:02.800
I've never felt so labelled
as I do here in Portugal.

72
00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:08.640
A woman, a foreigner, an engineer,

73
00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:14.280
a vegetarian, a world saviour,
and she also sorts the trash.

74
00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:19.520
It's like I'm walking around with
something written on my forehead.

75
00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:22.680
Alien, a foreign body.

76
00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:25.920
In that sense, it's been difficult.

77
00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:30.760
Maybe foreigners
aren't accepted after all.

78
00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:35.200
Or maybe Eastern Europeans
aren't accepted.

79
00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:38.920
I remember that
before I moved to Portugal,

80
00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:42.680
a friend from university
arranged for me to meet

81
00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:45.640
a Ukrainian woman from Portugal.

82
00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:49.080
So I could ask her
about life in Portugal.

83
00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:53.680
After a long chat, she told me
that Liisa, I wish you success

84
00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:56.240
and that everything goes
smoothly for you.

85
00:06:56.320 --> 00:07:00.280
But know that you can learn
100% Portuguese,

86
00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:06.840
adopt their culture and customs,
take part in everything.

87
00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:08.920
But they will never accept you,

88
00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:13.080
you will still remain
an Eastern European woman.

89
00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:22.320
My biggest challenge in Switzerland
was definitely settling in here.

90
00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:29.000
As an Eastern European, so to speak,
because people have prejudices.

91
00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:33.480
Many people don't know that Estonia
is a member of the European Union.

92
00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:39.240
They are surprised when they hear
that we don't speak Russian.

93
00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:43.120
We have our own language, Estonian.

94
00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:49.440
But it only gives me
the opportunity to educate them.

95
00:07:53.560 --> 00:08:00.240
Also, in my field, I had to
constantly fight prejudices

96
00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:06.480
that I had brains under my blonde hair.

97
00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:14.520
It would probably be harder if we came
from Africa or some other country.

98
00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:19.800
There are even some...
one guy from Peru, for example.

99
00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:22.320
For example, he was sometimes
not allowed into a nightclub

100
00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:25.160
because he has a bit darker skin.

101
00:08:25.240 --> 00:08:27.160
It's much harder for them.

102
00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:29.840
Coming from Northern Europe,
it's very easy for us.

103
00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:35.960
Absolutely. If you're fair-skinned,
you're more of a tourist to them.

104
00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:39.000
All doors are open.

105
00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:45.000
Eastern Europeans have a very nice
life here, compared to Africans.

106
00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:06.920
My biggest problem at the moment,
or the thing that scratches my heart,

107
00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:09.240
is perhaps homesickness.

108
00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:13.640
Talking to other Estonians
who have come to England,

109
00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:17.120
it seems to me that
it's like a pattern.

110
00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:20.560
At first you come abroad
with great excitement.

111
00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:26.960
Everything here is new and interesting,
and of course difficult at times.

112
00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:32.520
And maybe the first few years are nice.

113
00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:35.840
But then you start to get this
nagging feeling in your heart

114
00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:40.400
that something is pulling you
back to your homeland.

115
00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:46.640
Typically we go back to Estonia.
Maybe for a year, maybe for a couple.

116
00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:51.600
And then we usually come back abroad.

117
00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:58.200
I'm definitely feeling
homesick right now.

118
00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:08.080
The only guilt I feel is that

119
00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:13.280
I'm not there for my family,

120
00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:16.240
that I'm too far away.

121
00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:29.520
I'm not there when
they need me the most.

122
00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:40.360
You're pretty much left out
of your life, which you have at home.

123
00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:45.560
Your friends' lives and your parents
and all that are somewhere else.

124
00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:51.200
That's why I think
the salaries here are so high,

125
00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:59.360
they compensate you for the time
you sacrifice here for them.

126
00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:05.360
I have not yet met anyone,
any Estonian,

127
00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:10.680
who would definitely stay here
in Dubai for the rest of their lives.

128
00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:29.720
For me, it has been an eye-opening
and world-view-expanding experience.

129
00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:34.320
Now I look back and see that
I was like this in Estonia...

130
00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:37.240
Now I am like this...

131
00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:44.080
This is the kind of experience that
I would actually recommend to everyone.

132
00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:47.920
Maybe it's me,
that I come from a small place,

133
00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:50.840
I'm from Paide and Estonia is small.

134
00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:56.280
My brain was small, the world
was small, but coming to live here...

135
00:11:56.360 --> 00:12:00.560
Although we've travelled a lot,
we've seen the world, but...

136
00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:05.520
Coming to live here is something else.
- Yes. It was like...

137
00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:08.640
Eye-opening.
- Yeah. Absolutely.

138
00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:18.120
All these normal things that you
take for granted in Estonian life,

139
00:12:18.640 --> 00:12:22.480
to have them here,

140
00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:24.920
you have to work much harder.

141
00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:30.840
In order to find friends, to have...
I don't know, whatever.

142
00:12:31.320 --> 00:12:36.400
What probably made this
whole thing so cool or awesome

143
00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:43.480
is that in Estonia
your comfort zone is so wide.

144
00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:47.160
Being in there all the time
and here you actually...

145
00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:49.520
You're always in a discomfort zone.
- Yes.

146
00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:00.760
GENERATION BEYOND BORDERS

147
00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:05.280
NEW COUNTRY,
NEW OPPORTUNITIES

148
00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:28.920
Translated by Piret Õunapuu
Film Tower
